OL,3,AFrom Paris to DC - why offices are
OL,4,Abeing turned into apartments
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Roland Cubin walks you round what
OL,7,Fwill eventually be a new Parisian
OL,8,Fapartment you have to use your
OL,9,Fimagination.
OL,11,F"Here you will be in the kitchen, and
OL,12,Fhere is the bathroom," says the deputy
OL,13,FCEO of French real estate company
OL,14,FGroupama Immobilier.
OL,16,FIt all sounds appealing, an upmarket
OL,17,Fflat in the west of Paris, but
OL,18,Fpresently the space doesn't look like
OL,19,Fone at all. That's because it's
OL,20,Fcurrently a corner of one floor of a
OL,21,Fnine-storey office building called Le
OL,22,FDiamant, where 1,800 people work.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
FL,113,105,200,300,0,100
